        "Office of the Commissioner",
        "Office of the Chief Scientist"
      ],
      "regulatory_action_type": "guidance_update",
      "deadline": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c3e357dc-f13e-47c8-9c90-f677e5417178",
      "item_id": "93d241b8-3653-4c2e-9324-0d6185c19eca",
      "summary": "The FDA issued a Guidance for Industry to assist with the statutory requirements for cosmetic product facility registrations and product listings under MoCRA. The guidance explains who is responsible for submitting, what information to include, and how/when to submit. Three new FAQs in Appendix B (Q20-22) have been distributed for comment, with a deadline of January 13, 2025.",
      "key_regulations": [
        "MoCRA"
      ],
      "key_entities": [
        "Food and Drug Administration",
        "Office of the Commissioner",
        "Office of the Chief Scientist"
      ],
      "regulatory_action_type": "guidance_update",
      "deadline": "2025-01-13"
    },
    {
      "id": "58e9c325-7c7d-4302-a8c5-9425d3504959",
      "item_id": "d462bc94-474d-4e4f-ab52-d51fe83ce77d",
      "summary": "The FDA issued a warning letter to Brands International Corporation, a Canadian drug manufacturer, for significant CGMP violations and for limiting and delaying an FDA inspection in June 2024. Key violations include failure to investigate customer complaints of mold contamination in its \"Kissable Oatmeal Daily Moisturizing Body Lotion,\" failure to test incoming raw materials like glycerin for diethylene glycol (DEG) and ethylene glycol (EG), inadequate testing of finished products, poor facility conditions (pest control, improper storage), and an ineffective Quality Unit. The company's products are considered adulterated, and the firm was placed on Import Alert 66-40. The FDA requires a corrective action plan within 15 working days. The letter also notes that the firm's cosmetic products may be adulterated and subject to MoCRA.",
      "key_regulations": [
        "21 CFR Part 210",
        "21 CFR Part 211",
        "FD&C Act Section 501"
      ],
      "key_entities": [
        "Brands International Corporation",
        "Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER)"
      ],
      "regulatory_action_type": "cgmp_violation",
      "deadline": "2024-12-17"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf9c3a1d-d9ba-4cf9-8a31-34018b375aee",
      "item_id": "e6aa2c7c-2156-4722-b98b-05cc28307437",
      "summary": "The FDA released a congressionally mandated report under the Modernization of Cosmetics Regulation Act of 2022 (MoCRA) evaluating PFAS in cosmetic products. The report found insufficient toxicological data to definitively determine the safety of most PFAS, underscoring significant data gaps. The FDA will continue to monitor the issue and address data gaps, but no specific federal regulations prohibiting PFAS in cosmetics currently exist.",
      "key_regulations": [
        "Modernization of Cosmetics Regulation Act of 2022",
        "MoCRA"
      ],
      "key_entities": [
        "FDA",
        "CDC",
        "EPA",
        "U.S. Department of Health and Human Services"
      ],
      "regulatory_action_type": "administrative",
      "deadline": null
    },
    {
      "id": "60d70851-8666-4c6c-87ff-2dcb65e5c671",
      "item_id": "ea701a12-f04f-499d-8eef-4f692634dc8e",
      "summary": "The FDA issued a warning letter to Turkish manufacturer Neva Global Grup Sanayi Ic Ve Dis Ticaret Anonim Sirketi for significant CGMP violations concerning their over-the-counter (OTC) drug products. The inspection revealed failures in component identity testing, process validation, stability testing, and quality unit oversight. The firm was also noted to manufacture cosmetics and was reminded of MoCRA requirements. Consequently, the FDA has placed the company's products on Import Alert 66-40.",
      "key_regulations": [
        "21 CFR 210",
        "21 CFR 211",
        "21 CFR 211.84(d)(1)",
        "21 CFR 211.84(d)(2)",
